  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the relevant files. Summary of what the retrieval surfaced, most load-bearing first:\n\n1. **`react-dom`'s `ReactDOM.render`** \u2014 deprecated in React 18.2.0 (CHANGELOG.md, warns and runs in React 17 compat mode). CRA templates (`cra-template/template/src/index.js`, `cra-template-typescript/template/src/index.tsx`) already migrated to `ReactDOM.createRoot(...).render(...)` \u2014 **not** dead code, already updated.\n\n2. **`babel-preset-react-app/create.js`** \u2014 `runtime: opts.runtime || 'classic'` defaults to the legacy classic JSX transform (`React.createElement`) rather than the automatic runtime (`react/jsx-runtime`, added in React 16.14+/17+/18). `react-scripts/config/jest/babelTransform.js` and (presumably) `webpack.config.js` explicitly override this by feature-detecting `require.resolve('react/jsx-runtime')` and passing `runtime: 'automatic'`. So the classic default in `create.js` is vestigial fallback logic, not load-bearing against React 18.2.0 (which ships `react/jsx-runtime`) \u2014 load_bearing: false, kind: vestigial_shim.\n\n3. **`react-app-polyfill`** (`stable.js`, `ie9.js`, `ie11.js`, `jsdom.js`) \u2014 polyfills (`Object.assign`, `Promise`, `fetch`, etc.) that bridge browser-API gaps, not React internals directly; worth checking whether any target pre-`react/jsx-runtime` or `__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED` assumptions.\n\n4. **`react-dev-utils/refreshOverlayInterop.js`** and **`webpackHotDevClient.js`** \u2014 bridge `react-error-overlay` / Fast Refresh into webpack-dev-server; these depend on React DevTools hook conventions (`__REACT_DEVTOOLS_GLOBAL_HOOK__`) rather than `__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED` directly \u2014 no confirmed dead reference found.\n\n5. **`react-dom/test-utils`** (`ReactTestUtils.js`) still pulls `ReactDOM.__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED` in React 18.2.0 itself \u2014 this is React's own internal use, not something CRA references directly (CRA's default templates use Testing Library, not `react-dom/test-utils`, in `setupTests.js`).\n\nNo hard-broken (load-bearing-but-removed) references were found \u2014 CRA v5.0.1 was already updated for React 18's `createRoot` API and automatic JSX runtime detection. The one confirmed **vestigial** dead-code candidate is the `classic` default fallback branch in `babel-preset-react-app/create.js`, superseded by the auto-detection wrapper in the jest/webpack configs.",
